; implies_spin_model: IMPLIES on a spin {-1, +1} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; IMPLIES writes an implication penalty from variable 0 to variable 1, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which fails for spin variables
; and for integer variables with k > 2. The check follows the declared domain
; (only a model allocated by BQMX passes), so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has IMPLIES raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
SQMX r0          ; spin model, 4 variables
PUSH 0           ; i
PUSH 1           ; j
PUSH 5           ; penalty
IMPLIES r0
HALT
